course: dictionary
lesson: 1181
title: Brother, and what else it can mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A brother is a boy or man who has the same parents as you. In «Teenage brothers need space», the word is a person in a family, and the word teenage tells you his age. Context clues like older, elder or little tell you about age, and «my mum cares for my brother» shows that a mum and her child are in the family.
explain: Brother can also mean a close male friend, or a member of a group, like a monk. «And you, you will come too, young brother» uses brother as a way of speaking to someone close. Read the whole sentence to see whether it means a family member or something else.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so check which one fits. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense. A dictionary gives you every meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to choose.
fact: A brother is a boy or man who has the same parents as you.
fact: A half-brother shares only one parent with you.
fact: A stepbrother is the son of your stepparent.
fact: The plural of brother is brothers; an old plural is brethren.
fact: A legend says three brothers, Kyi, Shchek and Khoryv, and their sister Lybid founded a city; it is a legend, like Romulus and Remus for Rome.
exercise: A brother is? | A grown-up teacher at school | *A boy or man who has the same parents as you | A type of bird | A girl who lives next door
exercise: «The elder brother, who had stayed at home, was angry that the father celebrated.» Find and copy one word that tells you the brother is older. | *elder | celebrated | home | father
exercise: A stepbrother is? | A boy who shares only one parent with you | A boy in your class | Your twin cousin | *The son of your stepparent
test: What is a half-brother? | *A boy who shares only one parent with you | A boy who is taller than you | Two boys who are twins | A brother who lives far away
test: In the legend, what is the name of the sister? | Shchek | Khoryv | *Lybid | Kyi
exam: What can brother also mean, besides a family member? | A school timetable | A kind of mountain | *A close male friend or a member of a group, like a monk | A large brown bear
